Training data
-------------

The released weights were trained on the following datasets. The datasets themselves are not
part of this repository.

- Multilingual LibriSpeech (MLS), CC BY 4.0.
  V. Pratap, Q. Xu, A. Sriram, G. Synnaeve, R. Collobert. "MLS: A Large-Scale Multilingual
  Dataset for Speech Research." Interspeech 2020. https://www.openslr.org/94/
- LibriSpeech, CC BY 4.0.
  V. Panayotov, G. Chen, D. Povey, S. Khudanpur. "Librispeech: an ASR corpus based on public
  domain audio books." ICASSP 2015. https://www.openslr.org/12/
- MUSAN, CC BY 4.0.
  D. Snyder, G. Chen, D. Povey. "MUSAN: A Music, Speech, and Noise Corpus." arXiv:1510.08484,
  2015. https://www.openslr.org/17/
- VoxPopuli, CC0 1.0.
  C. Wang et al. "VoxPopuli: A Large-Scale Multilingual Speech Corpus for Representation
  Learning, Semi-Supervised Learning and Interpretation." ACL 2021.
- Mozilla Common Voice, CC0 1.0. https://commonvoice.mozilla.org/
- Synthetic speech generated with Google Gemini TTS.

No changes were made to the licensed datasets other than resampling, cutting and mixing them
for training.

Third-party software
--------------------

At runtime Hark uses eSpeak NG (GPL-3.0-or-later) for phonemization, through the piper-tts
package (GPL-3.0-or-later). Both are installed as separate packages and are included in the Docker image
and the Home Assistant app image. Their source code is available at
https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng and https://github.com/OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl.

The Hark logo uses the Outfit typeface (SIL Open Font License 1.1), see docs/brand/README.md.
